/* book: lead: Micro sensors are built on a silicon wafer by adding thin layers and removing them in patterns. Lithography draws the pattern, etching cuts it, and deposition fills or coats it. Bulk micromachining uses a wet etch that stops on crystal planes; surface micromachining uses a sacrificial layer that is dissolved to free a structure. The process choice fixes the shape, the material and the cost. Pressu */
/* book Figure 5.6.1: The back-side KOH etch stops on the 54.74° (111) planes, so the 505 µm deep pit grows outward by 357 µm on each side between the diaphragm and the mask. A 1000 µm diaphragm therefore needs a 1714 µm mask opening and about 361 min at 1.4 µm/min. */
