/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - A micro-fabrication recipe is a loop.
   - Etch removes material; deposition adds it.
   - d is etch depth in micrometres (µm); r is etch rate in µm/min; t is etch time in min.
   - Bulk micromachining removes silicon from the wafer body.
   - Deep reactive ion etching (DRIE) is a dry process that alternates etching and polymer passivation.
   - Surface micromachining, also called the sacrificial-layer process, builds on top of the wafer.
   - LIGA (X-ray lithography and electroplating) makes tall metal parts with vertical walls.
   - Thermal oxidation grows SiO2 by consuming silicon at 900-1100 °C.
   - After processing, the wafer is bonded to glass by anodic bonding or glass frit, diced into chips, attached to a package and sealed.
   - The same steps make medical devices.
*/
